  "starterCode": "# BPE Training — reconstructed educational contract\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solution(words, num_merges):\n    # TODO: implement the operation described in the problem statement\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **BPE Training** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nfrom collections import Counter\ndef solution(words, num_merges):\n    # Educational byte/character-level BPE: repeatedly merge the most frequent adjacent pair.\n    vocab=[list(w) for w in words]\n    merges=[]\n    for _ in range(max(0,int(num_merges))):\n        pairs=Counter(pair for token in vocab for pair in zip(token,token[1:]))\n        if not pairs: break\n        best=max(pairs, key=lambda p:(pairs[p],p))\n        merged=best[0]+best[1]\n        new_vocab=[]\n        for token in vocab:\n            out=[]; i=0\n            while i<len(token):\n                if i+1<len(token) and (token[i],token[i+1])==best:\n                    out.append(merged); i+=2\n                else: out.append(token[i]); i+=1\n            new_vocab.append(out)\n        vocab=new_vocab; merges.append([best[0],best[1],merged])\n    return merges\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
